## 3\'964. `cuisines` and `cafe_cuisines`\
\
Cuisine is multi-valued in the current CSV and can be used in Explore filters, so keep it separate rather than comma-joining values in the cafe row.\
\
- `cuisines`: `cuisine_id INT UNSIGNED` PK, `name VARCHAR(120)` UNIQUE.\
- `cafe_cuisines`: `cafe_id`, `cuisine_id`, with a composite primary key and foreign keys to `cafes` and `cuisines`.\
\
## 5\'966. `amenities` and `cafe_amenities`\
\
This supports both the existing checkboxes and custom CMS amenities.\
\
- `amenities`: `amenity_id INT UNSIGNED` PK, `name VARCHAR(100)` UNIQUE.\
- `cafe_amenities`: `cafe_id`, `amenity_id`, `is_available TINYINT(1) NOT NULL`, composite primary key across `cafe_id` and `amenity_id`.\
\
In the CMS, show available amenities as Yes/No controls. \'93Add custom amenity\'94 adds a reusable row to `amenities`, then editors can set Yes or No for each cafe. Example names: Wifi, Indoor seating, Outdoor seating, Work friendly, Lunch, Dinner. This keeps amenity values in the database without requiring a new `cafes` column whenever an amenity is added.\
\
## 7. `cafe_images`\
\
One row per photo, so galleries can be reordered and edited in the CMS.\
\
| Column | Type | Notes |\
|---|---|---|\
| `image_id` | `INT UNSIGNED` PK, auto-increment | Image record |\
| `cafe_id` | `INT UNSIGNED` FK | Owning cafe |\
| `image_path` | `VARCHAR(500)` | Project-relative path, not image bytes |\
| `alt_text` | `VARCHAR(255)` NULL | Accessible description |\
| `sort_order` | `SMALLINT UNSIGNED` | Gallery order |\
| `is_cover` | `TINYINT(1)` | Marks the cover image |\
\
Only assign a photo to a cafe when it really belongs to that cafe; a randomly chosen catalog image should not be stored as its photo.\
\
## 8. `users` \'97 simple account login\
\
| Column | Type | Notes |\
|---|---|---|\
| `user_id` | `INT UNSIGNED` PK, auto-increment | Account ID |\
| `username` | `VARCHAR(50)` UNIQUE | Required, unique login/display name |\
| `phone_number` | `CHAR(10)` UNIQUE | Store the 10 digits as text, without country code |\
| `password_hash` | `VARCHAR(255)` | Store a PHP-generated password hash, never the plain password |\
| `role` | `VARCHAR(20)` | Defaults to `user`; set `admin` only for CMS accounts |\
| `created_at` | `DATETIME` | Account creation time |\
\
The PHP form should validate exactly 10 digits and check username/phone uniqueness. Use PHP `password_hash()` when saving and `password_verify()` when logging in. Do not make an account admin through the public signup form.\
\
